<section class="container section prose-page"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR FILES STAY YOURS</span><h1 class="page-title">Private by design. Honest by default.</h1>
<h2>Where files go</h2><p>Documents are stored outside the public web root. Local conversion engines also use private operating-system temporary workspaces and remove them after processing. Only the account that uploaded a document can access its status, preview and download. Administrators see operational counts, not a document browser. No external conversion API is used, and this application does not use your files to train models.</p>
<h2>How long files stay</h2><p>Downloads expire {{ config('conversions.retention_hours') }} hours after submission. Scheduled cleanup removes files and preview data every ten minutes. Expired conversion metadata is removed after another seven days. You can delete a document and its history sooner, except while a conversion is actively processing. Infrastructure backups require their own retention policy.</p>
<h2>What we store</h2><p>Account name, email, hashed password, document filename, size, checksum, conversion status, private storage identifiers and bounded result previews. Minimal per-account submission counts enforce the daily quota even after history deletion; these counts contain no filenames or document content and are removed after two days or account deletion. Operational logs record conversion IDs and error categories rather than document contents. Audit events record administrator actions. Local development mail logs contain authentication links and must remain private.</p>
<h2>What conversions can change</h2><p>{{ App\Services\Conversions\FormatRegistry::warning() }} Review output before using it for financial, legal or other consequential work. No conversion is guaranteed to preserve an unsupported feature.</p>
<h2>Your account controls</h2><p>You can export account and conversion metadata or permanently delete your account and stored documents from Account settings. Deletion requires your password and is blocked during active processing. Administrative audit records retain the event without the deleted account ID.</p>
<h2>Before production use</h2><p>This is a staged release, not a certification of regulatory compliance. Malware scanning and hardened process isolation are not implemented yet. Do not deploy publicly until these controls, TLS, mail delivery, monitoring, backup policy and an organization-specific privacy notice have been reviewed.</p>
